summary:
- topic: AI Steering Committee Report
  text: The AI Steering Committee presented its initial findings, recommending the
    adoption of 'Magic School AI' for teachers and a phased approach to AI competency
    training for staff and students. The committee emphasized the importance of ethical
    AI use and integrating it into the curriculum, with ongoing work planned.
- topic: South Portland High School Performance Data
  text: South Portland High School reported positive trends in student data, including
    a 6.8% decrease in chronic absenteeism (from 42.3% to 35.5%) and a 66% reduction
    in out-of-school suspensions. Course failure rates also decreased to 4.4%, indicating
    improved student engagement and academic outcomes.
- topic: Facility Improvement Bond Proposal
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina outlined a $16.2 million bond proposal
    for critical facility upgrades. This includes $3 million for enhanced school security,
    $1 million for deferred maintenance (such as roof and window repairs), and $12.2
    million for a high school stadium complex.
- topic: High School Stadium Complex Details
  text: The proposed stadium complex would feature advanced, recyclable artificial
    turf (Iron Turf with Brockfill infill) to enhance playability, extend usability,
    and reduce maintenance challenges associated with natural grass. The superintendent
    highlighted the benefits of increased field availability and safety for student-athletes
    and the community.
- topic: Public and Board Discussion on Stadium Complex
  text: Public comments overwhelmingly supported the stadium complex, citing issues
    with current field conditions, frequent cancellations, safety concerns, and the
    desire for modern facilities. Some board members expressed reservations about
    the environmental impact and long-term costs of artificial turf, advocating for
    consideration of natural grass alternatives.
- topic: Referendum Approval for City Council
  text: The Board voted to send three separate bond referendums to the City Council
    for the November 2024 ballot. These include $3 million for school security, $1
    million for deferred maintenance, and an amended $12.3 million for the high school
    stadium complex, explicitly including synthetic turf fields.
- topic: New Administrator Introductions
  text: 'The meeting included the introduction and welcome of new administrators:
    Allison Hopkins as the new Principal at Dyer Elementary School and Ben Donaldson
    as the Assistant Principal at South Portland High School. Both expressed excitement
    about joining the district and supporting students and staff.'
